.TH IAD\-FLEX\-ROW 3 "" "iced-adaptive-design 0.1.0" "iced-adaptive-design Manual"
.SH NAME
flex_row \- A two\-item flex line with flex\-wrap semantics, used by every row
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
FlexRow::new(main: impl Into<Element<'a, M, Theme>>, aside: impl Into<Element<'a, M, Theme>>)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
A two\-item flex line with \fBflex\-wrap\fR semantics, used by every row.
.PP
\fBmain\fR (prefix + title) and \fBaside\fR (the suffix control) share a line while \fBmain\fR keeps at least \fBmain_basis\fR px; when they can't, \fBaside\fR wraps to its own line below, like CSS \fBflex\-wrap: wrap\fR. This avoids the title being crushed (or the control overlapping it) in narrow windows.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.TP
.B FlexRow::new(main: impl Into<Element<'a, M, Theme>>, aside: impl Into<Element<'a, M, Theme>>)
\fBmain\fR takes the leftover space on the first line; \fBaside\fR is the control.
.SH PROPERTIES
Builder methods, chained after the constructor.
.TP
.B \&.spacing(gap: f32)
Space between \fBmain\fR and \fBaside\fR on one line.
.TP
.B \&.line_spacing(gap: f32)
Space between the two lines when wrapped.
.TP
.B \&.main_basis(px: f32)
The minimum width \fBmain\fR keeps on the first line; below it, \fBaside\fR wraps.
.TP
.B \&.aside_basis(px: f32)
The width \fBaside\fR takes while sharing a line. Needed for \fBFill\fR\-width controls (sliders, entries), which have no natural width to measure.
.TP
.B \&.aside_align(a: Horizontal)
Where \fBaside\fR sits on its own line when wrapped with \fBCollapseBehavior::Flex\fR: \fBLeft\fR (start) or \fBRight\fR (end edge, \fBflex\-end\fR). While sharing a line it is always pinned to the end.
.TP
.B \&.collapse(c: CollapseBehavior)
What happens to \fBaside\fR when it wraps (see \fBCollapseBehavior\fR).
